        "orario": "17:30",
        "timestamp": 1775230200,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. French-owned CMA CGM container ship passes Strait of Hormuz Issued on: 03/04/2026 - 17:30 Modified: 03/04/2026 - 17:36 A container ship belonging to French shipping group CMA CGM has passed through the Strait of Hormuz, ​MarineTraffic vessel ‌tracking data shows, in a sign that Iran may not consider France ⁠a hostile nation. It is the first French-owned vessel to ‌make it through the channel since US-Israeli attacks began on Iran at the end of ⁠February. Until the war led to the effective closure of the Strait, it was the route for about a fifth of global oil and liquefied natural gas supplies. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert tells us more. 03/04/2026 Artemis II astronauts rocket toward the moon after spending a day around Earth 03/04/2026 Artemis II: Astronauts send first pictures of Earth as rocket leaves orbit 03/04/2026 Science Strikes hit Lebanon as Israel vows to occupy swathe of south after war 03/04/2026 8 killed, 95 wounded in US-Israeli attacks on Iran bridge 03/04/2026 Iran`s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps says it struck US F-35 jet 03/04/2026 The fight for mineral data in DRC: Belgian museum, US mining firm at odds over archive maps 03/04/2026 Trump fires Pam Bondi as US attorney general 03/04/2026 Storm batters Greece, killing one, flooding homes and disrupting travel 03/04/2026"
